            <ArticleTitle>Prolonged survival of a patient with left ventricular pseudoaneurysm following myocardial infarction and mitral valve replacement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>577-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a patient with left ventricular pseudoaneurysm following acute myocardial infarction. Survival for 2 years following diagnosis, despite the large size of the aneurysm, and subsequent management with cardiac transplantation represent unusual and interesting aspects of this complication of myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
